From fa29025e11c82fc7b0324fd68f23689aa165cef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): fuse rank-major shards in mhc.post and engram
 post-gate

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.

Rationale:
1. Extend mhc.post (post_streams) and engram_post_gate /
   engram_post_gate_blocked (_reconstruct_stream) with a compile-time world
   dimension and T.StridedTensor input declarations so SP prefill
   RankOrderParts ([world, rows, hidden] BF16) are summed in FP32 directly
   inside the consumer kernel without launching an intermediate
   previous_output.sum() kernel, reducing SP prefill boundary latency across
   2 GB10 boots by up to -29.64% on TP3 and -30.07% on TP4 for mhc.post and
   up to -11.39% for engram_post_gate_blocked.
2. In Engram.forward and Engram.declare_kernels on non-SP TP steps
   (sp_rows is None and tp_size > 1), all-gather wkv.local_product(rows) along
   dim=0 ([tp_size, num_tokens, block_cols]) and pass the rank-major tensor
   directly to engram_post_gate_blocked / engram_gate_blocked, eliminating
   concat_rank_shards and contiguous slice copies and reducing non-SP TP
   boundary latency by -10.89%..-79.41% on TP3 and -11.65%..-60.42% on TP4.

Quality:
Exact FP32 accumulation of rank-major shards inside _reconstruct_stream and
post_streams and bit-identical torch.equal output on non-SP TP Engram blocked
gating (matching rank-major shard indexing [rank, row, col_offset]).

Tests:
39/39 TileLang Engram + PDL tests, 11/11 model Engram tests, and 186/186 SP
prefill + L2 tests pass across 2 GPU boots on GB10 with 0 PDL violations.

Upstream status:
Adapted from source-fork norm-projection-boundaries (356d8fd5f) for candidate
1107.
